# Eluge, the Shoreless Sea's enters trigger resolves without Eluge (CR 113.7a, 603.4) and its land stays an Island once Eluge is
# gone: "It's an Island ... for as long as it has a flood counter on it" lasts as long as the counter, not as long as Eluge (CR
# 611.2b; ruling 2024-07-26: "stays an Island until the flood counter is removed, even if Eluge leaves the battlefield"). Turn 3:
# Eluge (Black Lotus and an Island) enters a 2/2 (two Islands) and targets Bot2's Plains; Bot2 answers with Swords to Plowshares, so Bot1 gains
# 2, Eluge's power as it last existed (CR 608.2h). The trigger still floods the Plains, which is an Island in addition to a Plains
# (CR 205.1b) and taps for {U} (CR 305.6) for Bot2 on its next turn, with Eluge long in exile.

